{"id":"sw-3a604e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@MBPM1X.local\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:33:24.259653Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-3a604e","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a138136c-3c5c-4a36-ac4d-a064a781a1c7","text":"**Summary** — Wrote `docs/DESIGN.md`: 8 numbered decisions (D1–D8) with rationale and revisit-conditions, subsystem architecture (world model, bricks/hot-cold DAG, raymarching/SSE, editing/op-log, streaming, destruction pipeline, GI, worldgen), a Nanite/Lumen adoption map, milestone table linking all 8 epics, and risks/deferred knobs.\n\n**Rationale** — Single canonical definition of the board's shared vocabulary (brick pool, op log, TLAS, anchor, hot/cold) so stories stay short; decision table format so future changes are diffs against explicit revisit-conditions rather than silent drift.\n\n**Decisions made** — Framed M3↔M4 ordering as soft (editing can start against un-compacted bricks); set initial world-data VRAM target at ≤2 GB (~500k bricks) as a starting budget, not a commitment; scoped notes.md as inherited background rather than duplicating its analysis.\n\n**Status** — Doc complete on branch `sw-3a604e-write-technical-design-document-docs-design-md`, uncommitted, ready for review. No tests applicable. Walkthrough to follow after review per workflow."},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:35:58.489033Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-3a604e","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"updated","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:43:23.247875Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-0656de","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Water as a first-class world feature, in two tiers (DESIGN.md D9):\n\n**Tier 1 — still water (early representation, reserved from M1)**: oceans, ponds, lakes are ordinary voxel material — generated by the water table in the volumetric generator, DAG-compressible, persisted through existing paths. Rendering adds one transmission segment to the raymarcher: refract at the surface, continue the march, tint by traversed depth (Beer–Lambert), reflections from the screen-space + cone-traced lighting stack.\n\n**Tier 2 — flowing water (sim, late)**: waterfalls, currents, basin filling. Affected bricks are promoted into an **active-sim set** carrying an auxiliary level/flow channel — the hot/cold pattern again: extra state only where water moves, GPU cellular update, demoted to plain material when settled. This is notes.md's \"GPU fluid dynamics via cellular occupancy\".\n\n**Exit criteria**: swim in a generated pond with refraction and reflections; a waterfall flows; a channel dug to a pond fills with water.","labels":["epic","water"],"sort_order":"ae","title":"Water: fluid representation, transmission rendering, cellular flow"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:43:28.396714Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-7dd08f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Atmosphere is where the raymarcher wins for free (DESIGN.md D10): volumetric fog and god rays are *accumulation along the primary march we already perform* — sample fog density and sun visibility while walking the ray. Heterogeneous, voxel-shadowed light shafts with no froxel volumes and no separate system.\n\n**Scope**\n- Global weather state plumbed as engine uniforms from M0: wind vector, fog density, precipitation, time-of-day sun\n- Height/depth fog accumulated along the march; god rays via sun-visibility sampling\n- Volumetric cloud layer + sky model (feeds the GI sky term)\n- Rain: particles, surface wetness response, puddle accumulation (waits on Water tier 1 representation)\n- Wind: global field consumed by particles and per-instance vegetation sway (TLAS refit already runs per frame)\n\n**Exit criteria**: a foggy dawn with god rays through the trees; rain that wets surfaces and forms puddles; a cloudy sky that darkens the GI.","labels":["epic","rendering","weather"],"sort_order":"af","title":"Atmosphere \u0026 Weather: fog, god rays, clouds, rain, wind"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:43:32.262164Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-e282e9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Define still water as ordinary voxel material (renders/compresses/persists through existing paths) and the promotion mechanism: bricks with moving water enter an active-sim set carrying an auxiliary 8-bit level/flow channel, demoted back to plain material when settled. Same hot/cold pattern as editing — extra state only where water moves.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","water","engine"],"parent_id":"sw-0656de","sort_order":"ag","title":"Water representation: fluid materials + active-sim brick state channel"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:43:53.085515Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-cf89be","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"On hitting a water surface: refract, continue the march underwater, tint by traversed water depth (Beer–Lambert), exit or terminate on solid hit. Uses the continuation hook shaped in sw-30aa3c. Underwater camera case included.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","water","rendering"],"parent_id":"sw-0656de","sort_order":"ah","title":"Transmission segment in the raymarcher: refraction + Beer–Lambert depth tint"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:43:55.547389Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-db74ad","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Animated wave normals (noise-based, wind-modulated via weather uniforms), Fresnel blend of reflection and transmission. Reflections reuse the lighting stack: screen-space trace first, cone-traced mips as fallback.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","water","rendering"],"parent_id":"sw-0656de","sort_order":"ai","title":"Water surface shading: animated normals, screen-space + cone-traced reflections"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:43:57.988858Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-16bff2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"GPU cellular update over the active-sim set's level/flow channel: downhill flow, spreading, basin accumulation, settling → demotion. Edit integration: digging a channel to a pond promotes boundary bricks and the channel fills. notes.md's \"GPU fluid dynamics via cellular occupancy\". Deliberately v1 — believable, not physically exact.","estimate":8,"labels":["feature","water","simulation"],"parent_id":"sw-0656de","sort_order":"aj","title":"Cellular flow sim v1 on active bricks: waterfalls, currents, basin fill"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:44:00.67674Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-efea3e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Engine-level weather/environment state block (wind vector, fog density, precipitation intensity, sun direction/time-of-day) plumbed as uniforms from the start and surfaced in the egui overlay for live tweaking. Cheap plumbing that every later atmosphere/water story consumes.","estimate":2,"labels":["feature","weather","infra"],"parent_id":"sw-7dd08f","sort_order":"ak","title":"Global weather state uniforms: wind, fog density, precipitation, time-of-day"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:44:03.50071Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-58bc46","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Sample fog density along the ray during the march we already perform (height falloff + distance). No froxel volume, no separate pass. Can land alongside the M6 lighting epic — it shares the traversal accumulation hook (sw-30aa3c).","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","weather","rendering"],"parent_id":"sw-7dd08f","sort_order":"al","title":"Height/depth fog accumulated along the primary march"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:44:06.320454Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-437e6d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"In-scatter sun light along the primary ray, shadowed by the voxel world (cheap sun-visibility samples through coarse mips). Heterogeneous, geometry-aware light shafts — a natural raymarcher win over rasterizer post-process shafts.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","weather","rendering"],"parent_id":"sw-7dd08f","sort_order":"am","title":"God rays: sun-visibility sampling along the march"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:44:08.677219Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-f2e6ce","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Raymarched cloud layer (noise-based coverage driven by weather state) over a physical-ish sky model. Cloud coverage feeds the GI sky-visibility term so overcast skies darken the world coherently.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","weather","rendering"],"parent_id":"sw-7dd08f","sort_order":"an","title":"Volumetric cloud layer + sky model"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:44:10.559534Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-e5b644","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Wind-blown rain particles (collide via coarse occupancy), material wetness response (darkening/spec), puddles as shallow still-water voxels in surface depressions — depends on the water representation story for the fluid material.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","weather","gameplay"],"parent_id":"sw-7dd08f","sort_order":"ao","title":"Rain: particles, surface wetness, puddle accumulation"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:44:13.385293Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-3afd48","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Pooled GPU allocator for 16³ bricks (1.6 m at 10 cm voxels). Voxel = 8-bit palette index into a per-brick material palette. Free-list recycling; stable brick handles for the index to reference.\n\nLeave room for optional auxiliary per-brick channels (fluid level/flow for the active-sim set — DESIGN.md §10): layout and handles must not preclude attaching side-channel data to a brick later."},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:44:14.793819Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-30aa3c","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Shallow top-level index (grid or shallow tree) mapping world space → brick handles. Hierarchical DDA: coarse steps through empty space, descend into bricks, per-voxel DDA inside. Empty-space skipping is the core perf primitive.\n\nStructure the traversal loop so a hit can continue as a transmission segment (water refraction — DESIGN.md D9) and so per-step accumulation (fog/god rays — D10) can be added without rearchitecting. Implemented later, shaped now."},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:44:16.69649Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-00ae86","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Generator is a 3D density + material function, not a heightmap — underground must contain strata and caves so digging (sw-b146f7) has something to find. Deterministic from seed; generates bricks on demand.\n\nIncludes a water table: oceans, ponds, and slow rivers placed as still-water material voxels (DESIGN.md D9) so water exists in generated worlds from M1."},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:44:17.758924Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
