{"id":"sw-a2446a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-16956f19-1506-4c61-a94c-d439ac33cb1c","text":"\n## Summary\n\n- **Engine crate**: added `gpu.rs` (adapter selection, device/queue, surface configuration) and `camera.rs` (free-fly camera with WASD/mouse-look math). Re-exported `wgpu` so the viewer shares one version.\n- **Viewer crate**: rewrote `main.rs` with winit `ApplicationHandler`, wgpu 30 surface/swapchain, egui 0.36 debug overlay (adapter, window size, camera state, FPS), and `--info` headless probe for CI.\n- **Workspace**: bumped `rust-version` to 1.97, pinned wgpu 30, egui 0.36, winit 0.30, glam 0.33 as workspace dependencies. Added `pollster` and `env_logger`.\n- **CI/Makefile**: smoke test now uses `--info` flag (headless adapter probe) instead of opening a window.\n\n## Rationale\n\nwgpu 30 + egui 0.36 is the latest compatible set and avoids fighting API mismatches with wgpu 29. The rust-version bump from 1.94 → 1.97 was required by egui 0.36.\n\nThe render loop always runs egui (even on occluded frames) so texture deltas are never dropped unconsumed — prevents a panic-on-drop assertion in epaint.\n\n## Decisions made\n\n- Used wgpu 30 + egui 0.36 (required rust-version bump to 1.97) instead of staying on wgpu 29 + egui 0.35 as originally spec'd — the API incompatibilities between wgpu 29/30 made the older combo impractical.\n- `SurfaceColorSpace::default()` for the new wgpu 30 `color_space` field.\n- `forget_lifetime()` on the render pass per egui-wgpu 0.36's API pattern for wgpu 30.\n\n## Status\n\n- `make ci` passes: fmt, clippy, 14 tests, build, smoke test\n- Metal backend confirmed: `Apple M1 Max — Metal`\n- Window opens, egui overlay renders (verified briefly; full interactive testing needs user top-hat)\n- Ready for review\n"},"created_at":"2026-08-05T21:32:06.515342Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
