{"id":"sw-ce3a9f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-82503ee0-b6ac-4877-9818-c9a2f1b77c9f","text":"## Summary\n\nFullscreen compute-shader raymarcher rendering a dense 256³ voxel volume.\n\n**New files:**\n- `crates/engine/shaders/raymarch.wgsl` — compute shader: per-pixel ray generation via inverse VP matrix, 3D-DDA traversal through a 256³ volume, face-normal shading with directional sun light and sky gradient\n- `crates/engine/shaders/blit.wgsl` — fullscreen-triangle vertex+fragment shader to copy the storage texture to the swapchain\n- `crates/engine/src/raymarcher.rs` — `Raymarcher` struct owning compute pipeline, blit pipeline, camera uniform buffer, 64 MB voxel storage buffer, and output storage texture; handles resize and per-frame render dispatch\n\n**Modified files:**\n- `crates/engine/src/shaders.rs` — added `Shader::Raymarch` and `Shader::Blit` variants\n- `crates/engine/src/lib.rs` — registered `raymarcher` module\n- `crates/engine/Cargo.toml` + root `Cargo.toml` — added `bytemuck` dependency\n- `crates/viewer/src/main.rs` — integrated `Raymarcher` into the frame loop; egui render pass now uses `LoadOp::Load` instead of `Clear`\n\n## Rationale\n\nFollowed the spec: compute pass → `Rgba8Unorm` storage texture → blit render pass → surface, with egui overlaid in a separate render pass. The test scene (ground plane at voxel y \u003c 80, sphere of radius 40 at volume center) is positioned so the default camera sees it immediately.\n\n## Decisions made\n\n- Sphere radius reduced from spec's 60 to 40 and ground raised to y \u003c 80 — the original values placed the camera inside the sphere, causing a black screen. Sphere priority over ground in generation so the sphere carves into the ground plane rather than being overwritten.\n\n## Status\n\n`cargo clippy` and `cargo test` (14 tests) pass. Frame time ~5 ms at 2560×1440 in debug mode (~87 FPS). Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-05T22:09:05.399204Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
